      "id": "HCR-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-hilbert-cusp-rows",
      "title": "Small integral denominators and finitely many rational cusp matrices",
      "statement": "A fixed constant A works at every embedding for a single nonzero pair (c,b)∈𝒪², with |w(c)τ_w+w(b)|²≤A Im τ_w. There are a fixed finite S⊂SL₂(F) and B and, for each such pair, λ∈F× with |Nλ|≤B such that every unit multiple of λ(c,b) is the bottom row of r k with r∈S and k∈SL₂(𝒪).",
      "hypotheses": "F is a totally real number field for the small row, using all its real embeddings and strictly positive heights. The finite row completion holds for any number field. The row generates a nonzero integral ideal.",
      "correspondence": "The product of determinant-one archimedean blocks preserves lattice covolume. The numerator ideal may be nonprincipal. Completing a row uses its inverse ideal. Fix an adapted matrix for each class encountered before multiplying the row by a balancing unit.",
