    {
      "id": "HCR-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-hilbert-cusp-heights",
      "title": "Unit balancing gives a positive lower height at every real embedding",
      "statement": "For some fixed κ,t>0 every positive tuple τ has r∈S and k∈SL₂(𝒪) such that z_w=Im(r k τ)_w≥t and κ z_w≤z_v for all v,w. The common scale can be arbitrarily large.",
      "hypotheses": "F totally real, all real embeddings, positive imaginary parts, integral determinant-one k and finitely many rational determinant-one matrices r. Dirichlet’s logarithmic unit lattice and the bounded absolute norm of the row multiplier enter separately.",
      "correspondence": "The bottom row uses u⁻¹ before λ. The imaginary parts are therefore multiplied by |w(u)|². Their product is unchanged. Bounding the logarithmic deviations by L yields κ=exp(−4L). The source takes t=κ min(1,P) with P=1/(A^d B²).",
      "dependencies": [
        "HCR-01"
      ],
