    {
      "id": "HCR-04",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-isotropic-transverse",
      "title": "A compact transverse family transfers the shell bound to the unfolded integral",
      "statement": "For an adelic Hermitian group G with a chosen hyperbolic plane and isotropic-line stabilizer P, one compact C satisfies G=PC. A positive cutoff on C and Tonelli bound any nonnegative unfolded line count by a fixed constant times the shell volumes with uniform majorants on an enlarged compact transverse family.",
      "hypotheses": "Work over a CM extension, with a nondegenerate ambient form, its rational hyperbolic pair and the rational subgroup Γ∩P. The test is measurable, nonnegative and Γ∩P-invariant, and on each shell admits a uniform bound after multiplication on the right by the compact transverse cutoff support. The shell set covers P up to measure zero modulo its rational elements.",
      "correspondence": "Primitive-vector normalization, an explicit hyperbolic partner and compact lifting on a nonsingular rank-two Gram orbit yield G=PC. Compact cutoff averaging corrects for overlaps, and unfolding the count lands on (Γ∩P)∖G. G is integrated in its own Haar measure.",
